    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1525/S.12.1>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.12.1>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1525/S.12.1/text> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1525/S.12.1/texte> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1525> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1525/S.19/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "Exploitation renforcée de deux sources administratives :  \n\n- les fichiers de déclarations annuelles sur les bénéfices tels que BIC (bénéfices industriels et commerciaux), BNC (bénéfices non commerciaux), BA (bénéfices agricoles) transmis par la DGFiP ;  \n\n- les Déclarations Annuelles de Données Sociales (DADS) ;  \n\nCes deux sources administratives sont complétées par des enquêtes statistiques : l’Enquête Annuelle de Production (EAP) dans l’industrie, et l'Enquête Sectorielle Annuelle (ESA) pour les autres secteurs d’activité."@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1525/S.12.1/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "Comptabilité nationale, SSM, chercheurs"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1525/S.10.2/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "Insee Résultats"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1525/S.11.1>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.11.1>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1525/S.11.1/texte> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1525/S.11.1/text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1525> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1525/S.19>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.19>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1525/S.19/text> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1525/S.19/texte> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1525> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1525/S.19/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "Strengthened exploitation of two administrative sources:  \n\n- the files of income annual statements of enterprises: Industrial and Commercial Profits System (BIC), Non-Commercial Profits system (BNC) or Agricultural Profits (BA), coming from the DGFiP;  \n\n- the annual declarations of social data (DADS).  \n\nThese two administrative sources are completed by statistical surveys : the annual production survey (EAP) on industry, and the annual sectoral survey (ESA) for other sectors of activity."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1525/I.18.10/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "4.5 millions companies concerned by the scheme, approximately 2.9 millions belong to the field on which we realize the statistical surveys ESA and EAP."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1525/S.3.1/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "Main tax data: turnover, gross operating surplus (EBITDA), value added (VA), accounting result, fixed assets, sales margin, total employment, paid employment, self-employment, etc.\n\nAssociated ratios: turnover per employee, VA per employee, annual gross wage per employee, fixed assets per employee, total assets per employee, gross margin rate (EBITDA/VA), export rate etc.\n\nThe turnover's breakdown by activity, which allows the determination of the main activity (APE code)."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1525/S.3.4>
