    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1629/S.3.6/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "The population is composed of establishments with 20 or more employees, with at least 4 months of activity in 2015, and main activity code ('APET) corresponding to sections B and C (division 05 to 33), to group 383 (materials recovery),   \nexcluding: subclasses: 1013B, 1071B, 1071C, 1071D (commercial crafts), 2013A and 2446Z ;  \nexcluding divisions 05, 06 and 19;  \noutside group 091.  \n\nAbout 14,000 establishments were surveyed, including an extra-sample specific to 2015."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1629/S.1.5>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/simsv2/attribute/S.1.5>
                    "<p>Insee, 88 avenue Verdier,&nbsp; CS 70 058, 92 541 Montrouge Cedex.</p>"@fr , "<p>Insee, 88 avenue Verdier,&nbsp; CS 70 058, 92 541 Montrouge Cedex.</p>"@en ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1629> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1629/S.16/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "For the annual collection (including preparation): 3.5 FTE A, 10.5 FTE B and C. IT resources: 80 days. The postage budget is approximately 17,000 euros, and the telephone budget 2,400 euros.  \nThe median (rectified) response time is 35 minutes.  \nThe label committee also ensures that the survey does not place an excessive burden on respondents.  \nIn addition, other decisions were made to limit the burden on respondents:\n\n* the EACEI sample for \"conventional\" collection (wave 1) is renewed by half compared to that for EACEI 2014;\n* the part of the EACEI 2015 sample is negatively coordinated with the following surveys: CPSV18130, EMAGSA15, ECEIPE14, PV14_MONO, PV14_MULTI, ANT14, ANT14_3839, EAP14, CIS14, RPS16_TEST, RPS16, TPE15_R, TPE15_C, EDD14, CHALLENGES, TIC16_R, TIC16_C, ESA14_C, ESA14_R, SINE14_AUTO, SINE14₁;\n* collection is done electronically;\n* the sample of the extension collected at the end of the year (second wave) was not intended to be interviewed by a panel and was therefore drawn independently of the numbers of the previous surveys."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1629/S.13.1/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "The precision indicators (standard deviation, coefficient of variation, 95% confidence interval) take into account errors due to sampling, total non-response correction and calibration, but not the error related to partial non-response correction.  \n\nThe variables used for the EACEI 2015 precision calculations are :  \nBR_QAUP (quantity purchased in electricity)  \nDR_QAUP (quantity purchased in natural gas)  \nJR_QAUP (quantity purchased in butane-propane)  \nLR_QAUP (quantity purchased in heating oil)  \n\nThe indicators are as follows:  \nestimate of total  \ncoefficient of variation in percentage = 100 * s / total  \n\nThe results of the calculations are in the file \"Calculs de précision pour les variables cibles\"."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> ;
            <http://rdf.insee.fr/def/base#additionalMaterial>
                    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/901> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1629/S.17.2>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.17.2>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1629/S.17.2/texte> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1629/S.17.2/text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1629> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1629/I.18.10/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "La base de sondage est le répertoire Sirus (répertoire des unités statistiques).  \nLa méthode d'échantillonnage est un plan stratifié par NTE (Nomenclature de Travail de l'EACEI), tranches d’effectif salarié, et région.  \nLes allocations sont optimisées sur le croisement NTE x Tranches d’effectifs, et sur la consommation nette d’énergie, en prenant en compte la moyenne des dispersions par strate des 3 dernières années. Les allocations sont exhaustives au-delà du seuil de 250 salariés et pour les strates de moins de 10 unités."@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
