                    "La période de collecte s'est étendue du 20 juin au 15 novembre 2017."@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/1112>
            a                        <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "Méthodologie de l'enquête annuelle sur les investissements pour protéger l'environnement (Antipol) 2018"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/language>
                    "fr" ;
            <http://purl.org/pav/lastRefreshedOn>
                    "0019-05-11"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
            <http://schema.org/url>  <https://www.insee.fr/fr/metadonnees/source/fichier/S.18.5.MET_ANTIPOL.pdf> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1838/S.3.1/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "Les thèmes abordés portent sur les investissements (matériels entièrement dédiés à la protection de l'environnement, achats d'équipements de production plus performants en matière environnementale...), les études (en vue d'un investissement ou réglementaires) et les dépenses courantes (collectées tous les 3 ans) destinées à protéger l'environnement.\n\nCes dépenses sont réparties selon les domaines concernés :  \n- eaux usées ;  \n- protection de l'air ;  \n- limitation des gaz à effet de serre ;  \n- déchets ;  \n- bruits et vibrations ;  \n- sols et eaux souterraines et de surface ;  \n- sites, paysages et biodiversité ;  \n- autres domaines."@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> ;
            <http://rdf.insee.fr/def/base#additionalMaterial>
                    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/1113> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1838/S.18.3/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "Internet with the possibility of using postal means upon demand.\n\nUnits of measure:  \n- The workforce of the establishment is requested on 31/12/2016 (EFF_ETAB), number of FTE dedicated to environnment (EFF_ENV): number of occupied people  \n- Studies and investments for environmental protection: thousands of euros  \n- The shares (PART_ACHAT, PART_ENVIR) and breakdown (IE, ID, IA, IG, IB, IS, IP, IR et TOT_PCT) : percentage (%)"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1838/S.10.3/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "Insee Focus and Insee Resultats are available on the insee.fr site."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1838/S.19/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "L'enquête répond au règlement européen relatif aux statistiques structurelles sur les entreprises (CE N°251/2009) du 11 mars 2009, demandant de fournir les dépenses de protection de l'environnement ventilées par domaine environnemental, par activité et par taille d'entreprise."@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1838/S.11.2/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "The survey shows a decrease in response rate: 81.8% (86.3% in the previous edition) because of the interrogation about included current expenditure.\n\nBefore any exploitation, it is also useful to assess the quality of the variables through their partial non-response rate and the confidence intervals provided in the survey quality indicators.\n\nThis year, the partial non-response rate is very higt for the variable RED_ASS_EPU. It stands at 22%.  \nThis variable should therefore be analysed with caution, as a significant proportion of the responses have therefore been imputed.\n\nThe variables AU_TA and COTIS have a partial non-response rate relatively hight. It stands at 9.1 %.\n\nThe other variables all have a partial non-response rate of less than 6%.\n\nIn terms of precision, the main numerical variables have the following coefficients of variation:  \nTotal amount of studies to protect the environment (TOT_ETUDE): 3.2%  \nTotal amount of specific investments (IT): 2.6%.  \nAmount of integrated environmental protection investments (I2): 6.2%.  \nAmount of operating and maintenance of equipments dedicated to environnment (TD): 2,0%.  \nAmount of current expenditure to protect environment (TOT_DEP_COUR): 1,3%.\n\nAccuracy degrades when one focuses on finer diffusion domains. In particular, the following sectors of activity have a coefficient of variation exceeding 30% and should be analysed with caution:  \n\nFor (TOT_ETUDE)  \nManufacture of vegetable and animal oils and fats  \nGrain processing; manufacture of starch products  \nProcessing and preserving of fish, crustaceans and molluscs  \nAutomotive industry  \nManufacture of animal feed  \nLeather and Footwear Industry  \nManufacture of bakery and pasta products\n\nFor (TI)   \nManufacture of animal feed  \nProcessing and preserving of fish, crustaceans and molluscs  \nManufacture of bakery and pasta products  \nClothing industry   \nRepair and installation of machinery and equipment  \nLeather and Footwear Industry  \nManufacture of vegetable and animal oils and fats  \nWoodworking and manufacture of articles of wood and cork, except furniture; manufacture of articles of straw and plaiting materials\n\nFor variable TI, the overseas region (97) is in the same case.\n\nFor (I2)    \nLeather and Footwear Industry    \nManufacture of animal feed  \nClothing industry   \nExtraction Coking and refining  \nGrain processing; manufacture of starch products  \nFurniture manufacturing    \nProcessing and preserving of fish, crustaceans and molluscs  \nFabrication de produits informatiques, électroniques et optiques\n\nFor variable I2, the overseas regions (97) and Corse (94) are in the same case.\n\nFor (TD)  \nLeather and Footwear Industry"@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1838/S.1.1>
