            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "The survey was conducted among people who attended an accommodation or free catering site at least once during the period between 15 January and 12 February 2001.\n\nA person is described as \"homeless\" on a given day if, on the previous night, he or she used an accommodation service or slept in a place not intended for habitation (street or makeshift shelter)."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1718/I.18.10/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "The sample is produced by three-stage sampling: conurbations, support services and survey days, and the users of these services.  \n\nIn June 1999, 80 conurbations were randomly sampled: a complete register of the accommodation and hot meal distribution services was compiled in these conurbations.  \n\nIn March 2000, a telephone survey of 2,800 organisations was conducted with a view to gathering additional information about the types and characteristics of the services on offer. A database of nearly 1,500 services was thus compiled.  \n\nThen, on the actual day of the survey (between January and February 2001), a third sampling level was applied: in general, 4 \"service provisions x day\". In practice, investigating the \"services provided\" actually amounted to investigating the beneficiaries of these services.  \n\nThe services to be surveyed were selected either by random sampling from the list of users of the service or, in the absence of such a list, according to the order in which users passed through a mandatory point: front door, exit door or the meal distribution table.  \n\nAll in all, INSEE surveyed 4,000 people aged 18 and over, in 80 conurbations in Metropolitan France, in order to obtain a representative sample of adults attending cooked meal distributions or accommodation services, in conurbations of more than 20,000 inhabitants.  \n\nAccompanying children were recorded but not questioned. It was only possible to contact people who had attended either an accommodation service or a cooked meal distribution service at least once during the week of the survey."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1718/S.18.2>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.18.2>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/frequence/P> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1718> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1718/S.3.6/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "People using accommodation services or distribution of cooked meals, French-speaking, aged 18 and over."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1718/I.20/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "L'enquête Sans-domicile 2001Insee Méthodes n° 116  \n<https://www.epsilon.insee.fr/jspui/handle/1/7294>"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1718/I.18.9>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.9>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/uniteEnquetee/I> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1718> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1718/S.18.3/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "Data collection was carried out by face-to-face interviews held from 15 January 2001 to 12 February 2001 in metropolitan France, conurbations of more than 20 000 inhabitants."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1718/S.3.4>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.3.4>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1718/S.3.4/text> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1718/S.3.4/texte> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1718> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1718/S.3.4/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "L'enquête aborde les thèmes suivants : situation vis-à-vis du logement, histoire résidentielle, ressources financières, aides personnelles, situation sur le marché du travail, formation, contacts sociaux, accès aux soins, histoire familiale."@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1718/I.18.8>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.8>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/modeCollecte/F> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1718> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1718>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#MetadataReport> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "Quality report: Survey about users of accommodation and hot meal distribution services - 2001"@en , "Rapport qualité : Enquête auprès des personnes fréquentant les lieux d'hébergement ou de restauration gratuite - 2001"@fr ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#target>
                    <http://bauhaus/operations/operation/s1267> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1718/S.19/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "L'enquête a été réalisée auprès des personnes ayant fréquenté au moins une fois entre le 15 janvier et le 12 février 2001 un lieu d'hébergement ou de restauration gratuite.\n\nUne personne est qualifiée de \" sans-domicile \" un jour donné si la nuit précédente elle a eu recours à un service d'hébergement ou si elle a dormi dans un lieu non prévu pour l'habitation (rue, abri de fortune)."@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
}

<http://rdf.insee.fr/graphes/qualite/rapport/1948> {
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1948/S.3.7>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.3.7>
                    <http://bauhaus/geo/territoireFrancais/franceMetropolitaine> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1948> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1948/S.3.4/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "L’indicateur synthétique du climat des affaires dans l’enquête décrit la composante commune des soldes d’opinion sur les perspectives générales des entreprises sur leur secteur, les intentions de commandes, les ventes passées, les effectifs passés et prévus, les prix de vente prévus, les stocks.\n\nL’indicateur de retournement de conjoncture est une variable qualitative qui n’est pas observée directement. L’indicateur se présente sous la forme d’une courbe, retraçant à chaque date la différence entre la probabilité que la phase conjoncturelle soit favorable et la probabilité qu’elle soit défavorable. Il évolue donc entre +1 et -1 : un point très proche de +1 (respectivement de -1) signale que l’activité est en période de nette accélération (respectivement de nette décélération). Les moments où l’indicateur est proche de 0 sont assimilés à des phases de stabilisation."@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1948/S.11.1/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "The monthly outlook survey inservices is part of the harmonised European Union programme of business and consumer surveys to which the 28 Member States of the European Union contribute.\n\nThus questionnaires, classifications and data processing methods have been harmonised to a large extent in the national institutes of the countries that have adopted this system.\n\nQuestions are formulated so that they can be answered quickly (most of the questions are qualitative with three response options expressed in the form \"higher, lower, stable\", or \"more than normal, normal, less than normal\")."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1948/I.18.12>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.12>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1948/I.18.12/texte> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1948/I.18.12/text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1948> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1948/S.3.1>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.3.1>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1948/S.3.1/texte> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1948/S.3.1/text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1948> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1948/S.1.7>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/simsv2/attribute/S.1.7>
                    "01 87 69 58 78"@fr , "01 87 69 58 78"@en ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1948> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1948/S.18.6/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "The published series are seasonally adjusted (CVS). Seasonality tests are carried out on all series. As a result, the published series are seasonally adjusted (CVS). A series that initially has no seasonal character is presented as a CVS series with zero coefficients and is equal to the gross series. The effects are estimated with the X13 and TramoSeats software under JDemetra+ (provided by Eurostat) at the level of aggregates specific to the NAF rev. 2 subclass survey. CVS indices for senior positions are obtained directly, not by aggregating the CVS indices that compose them."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/1162>
            a                        <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "Questionnaire 2020 des mois de janvier et juillet des autres entreprises"@fr ;
