            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/S.10.2/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "Les données sont publiées à la rubrique Insee Résultats sous insee.fr."@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/I.18.10>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.10>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/I.18.10/texte> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/I.18.10/text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1719> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/I.18.10/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "Il s'agit d'un sondage aléatoire simple stratifié en grappes selon des classes de taille croisées avec les secteurs économiques. Au dessus de certains seuils de taille – seuils de chiffre d’affaires et d’effectifs salariés –, variables avec les secteurs, le tirage est exhaustif."@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/I.6.3>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.6.3>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/statutEnquete/T> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1719> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/S.3.1/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "The themes addressed in the survey are as follows:   \n-The business's principal activity;  \n-The events occurring during the accounting year (merger-absorption, full transfert of assets, partial transfer of assets, split off);  \n-The details of the restructuring (increases and decreases in fixed assets);  \n-Tangible investments and sales;  \n-Employment (non-employeed staff, temporary staff, staff leased to other companies, etc.);  \n-Breakdown of turnover by product or detailed activity;  \n-Professional expenses (non-stored purchases, incorporated sub-contracting, etc.);\n\nSectoral characteristics such as:  \n- Breakdown of the turnover of the form of sales like company retail;  \n- Analysis of the customer base (breakdown of turnover by type of customer);  \n- Analysis of the providers retail;  \n- Other charges and external charges (general sub-contracting, rent and rental charges, maintenance expenses, etc.) for transport companies;  \n- Long-term assets, a for agri-food companies and agricultural cooperative;  \n- Work performed on existing or future buildings;  \n- Localisation of sites, work performed on existing or future buildings, type of work performed;  \n- The list of establishments registered on the Business Register Sirene, subcontracting capacity, financial leasing for forestry companies."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/documents/document/193>
            a                        <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label>
                    "Enquête Construction (Questionnaire 2016)"@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/language>
                    "fr" ;
            <http://purl.org/pav/lastRefreshedOn>
                    "2017-02-03"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
            <http://schema.org/url>  <https://www.insee.fr/fr/metadonnees/source/fichier/Questionnaire_esa2016_construction.pdf> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/S.10.2>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/S.10.2>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/S.10.2/text> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/S.10.2/texte> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1719> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/S.18.5/texte>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "Une chaîne de contrôles et redressements automatiques spécifique a été mise en œuvre. Cette chaîne assure en outre la cohérence des données de l'enquête avec les données fiscales de l'entreprise."@fr ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/fr> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/S.1.4>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/simsv2/attribute/S.1.4>
                    "<p>Head of Structural Business Statistics Section</p>"@en , "<p>Chef de la Division &eacute;laboration des statistiques annuelles d'entreprises</p>"@fr ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1719> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/S.18.4/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "The data and resultats are checked and validated by the ESANE teams in Nantes and Paris."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/I.18.10/text>
            a       <http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/Text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value>
                    "The sampling design is a two-stage stratified clustered simple ramdom sampling, according to strata defined by the size classes crossed with the economic sectors. Above given size thresholds – thresholds on tunover and on number of employees –, which are variable according to the economic sector, the strata are take-all strata."@en ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                    <http://bauhaus/codes/langue/en> .
    
    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/I.18.7>
            a       <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#ReportedAttribute> ;
            <http://bauhaus/qualite/simsv2fr/attribut/I.18.7>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/I.18.7/texte> , <http://bauhaus/qualite/attribut/1719/I.18.7/text> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/ns/sdmx-mm#metadataReport>
                    <http://bauhaus/qualite/rapport/1719> .
}

